{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PHASE 2 NOT EXECUTED — deliberately left for an operator decision. Reporting it rather than acting.\n\n836 comments remain across three issues that phase 1 did not touch: REB-1567 (418), REB-1931 (278), REB-2605 (140). They carry NO reconciler marker, so they fail the phase-1 authoritative identifier and were excluded as non-candidates throughout.\n\nEvidence they are bot echoes of the same bug, not human comments:\n- authored by the same single bot accountId as every marked comment (712020:6471376f-4e5e-4ed2-8c05-330827bc387e);\n- each body repeats ~139 times identically (REB-1567 has 4 distinct bodies across 418 comments; REB-1931 has 2 across 278; REB-2605 has 2 across 140);\n- each rendered body is exactly 32767 chars and ends in the reconciler's own constant _TRUNCATION_SUFFIX ' ... [truncated by reconciler]' (adapters/jira/comment_limits.py) — outbound truncation cut the body short and removed the trailing marker paragraph.\n\nA phase-2 rule is implemented and dry-run-tested behind --include-truncated (candidate = rendered text ends with _TRUNCATION_SUFFIX AND author.accountId == the bot accountId; same keep-oldest-per-distinct-body rule, so the one-surviving-copy invariant is unchanged). Dry run on REB-2605: 145 -> 7 kept, 138 deletions.\n\nIt was NOT run because the identifying rule is one I derived for this incident rather than the precedent's marker rule, and deletion is irreversible. There is also no urgency: all three issues sit at 145-430 comments, far below the 5000 cap, so comment sync is not blocked on them. Run with:\n  python cleanup.py REB-2605 REB-1931 REB-1567 --include-truncated            # dry run\n  python cleanup.py REB-2605 REB-1931 REB-1567 --include-truncated --execute  # after review\n\nSEPARATE FINDING worth its own ticket: the reconciler truncates outbound comment bodies at 32767 chars in a way that DROPS the RECONCILER_MARKER paragraph (the marker is appended after the body, so truncation cuts it off). That defeats the loop-breaker for any comment over the limit — such an echo is unrecognisable as the reconciler's own on the inbound side, and unrecognisable to cleanup tooling. Truncating to (limit - len(marker)) and re-appending the marker would fix it."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787267821305334001,"uuid":"a795d73d-9202-4262-9add-37d38944d30d"}